items.content:
@mert_gulsun @xeophon Businesses and enterprises should always have their own evals and make decisions largely based on that IMO

Public benchmarks are usually so general that they are more valuable to big labs and research, and provide some nudges for everyone to try things 

But it’s far too one sided at the moment towards benchmarks.  Benchmarks tell you very little about if a model is best for you!   I think it’s a marketing and communications problem by those who profit from benchmarks that mislead consumers

@mert_gulsun @xeophon In other words, public benchmarks should only be used for the top of funnel of decision making, “should I consider this new model?”

And then private evals should be used for the rest “Is this model actually good for my workflow or product to make a business impact?” 

Evals are time consuming so sometimes not feasible, but right now too many people using benchmarks for the whole funnel and as a singular point of decision making

